Post-installation steps for Slackware
-------------------------------------

1. Enable the TLP services

TLP and the TLP Profiles Daemon are independent services. Enable
their scripts with:

  # chmod +x /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp
  # chmod +x /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp-pd

Then add the following to /etc/rc.d/rc.local:

  if [ -x /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp ]; then
    /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp start
  fi
  if [ -x /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp-pd ]; then
    /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp-pd start
  fi

You may start them immediately with:

  # /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp start
  # /etc/rc.d/rc.tlp-pd start


2. Configuration

System configuration is read from:

  /etc/tlp.conf
  /etc/tlp.d/*.conf

A template is installed as /etc/tlp.conf.new for administrator
review.

For TLP 1.11 and newer, profile-specific settings use these suffixes:

  _PRF  performance profile
  _BAL  balanced profile
  _SAV  power-saver profile

The older `_AC` and `_BAT` names continue to work through runtime
translation. Use `tlp-stat --cdiff` to locate settings that should be
updated.


3. TLP Profiles Daemon

This package includes the TLP Profiles Daemon and its command-line
client. The daemon provides the power-profiles daemon interface
without requiring power-profiles-daemon or systemd.

The daemon requires the Slackware packages python3, pygobject3,
polkit, and dbus. The activation procedure is described in section 1.

The available profiles can then be inspected or changed with:

  $ tlpctl list
  $ tlpctl balanced

The `tlp-pd` daemon must be running for `tlpctl` to work.

4. Radio Device Wizard

The Radio Device Wizard (`tlp-rdw`) requires NetworkManager and can
enable or disable radio devices when network connections change.
Ensure that
`/etc/rc.d/rc.networkmanager` is enabled when using this feature.
It has no separate service; NetworkManager runs its dispatcher hook.

Configure it in `/etc/tlp.conf` using settings such as:

  DEVICES_TO_DISABLE_ON_LAN_CONNECT="wifi wwan"
  DEVICES_TO_DISABLE_ON_WIFI_CONNECT="wwan"
  DEVICES_TO_ENABLE_ON_LAN_DISCONNECT="wifi wwan"

Use the following commands to check or change the Radio Device
Wizard state:

  $ tlp-rdw
  # tlp-rdw enable
  # tlp-rdw disable

5. Notes for upgrades

If existing `/etc/tlp.conf`, `/etc/rc.d/rc.tlp`, or
`/etc/rc.d/rc.tlp-pd` files are present, new versions will be
installed as `.new` files. Review and merge changes as needed.
Files in `/etc/tlp.d/` are administrator-managed drop-ins and are
not overwritten.
